// dag/test/claim/service_endpoint_supply_module_resolve.dag — THE RUNG THIS CUT WAS MISSING.
//
// `test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_fixture_parse_test` reads fixture declarations back after a
// real parse, and `test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_emit_control` compiles fixture SOURCE
// TEXT through the emit check. Neither path DEMANDS a module that declares a parameter-bound endpoint
// as one of its own items, and that demand is the only place where `config { endpoint: <name> }` is
// resolved at all: resolution walks the service's minted `svc_endpoint` property, and with the
// admission removed the endpoint expression falls back to an ordinary module-scope name and this entry
// refuses with `error: undefined variable 'request_url'` at the authored position. So the assertion of
// this file is that its own entry resolves, and the boolean below is the reachable read-back that says
// WHY it resolved: the endpoint is still the authored variable, an `ExprVar` named `request_url`, not a
// literal the front end quietly substituted for it (DESIGN §5: no plausible output is fabricated).
//
// REVERSE CHECK, registered in the PR body: take the admission away from
// `v1.compiler.infer_service.service_endpoint_supply` and this entry stops resolving -- the refusal is
// the one above. The red half is already measured against the old rule: the pinned pre-change seed
// (`c469966f`) refuses exactly this spelling, at `endpoint: request_url`, while the same module with a
// module-level `data request_url: String` resolves -- which is what makes the binding, and not a
// module-scope lookup, the thing under test.
//
// The service below is written twice on purpose and the pairing is said, not assumed: as real module
// ITEMS (what makes the entry demand resolution), and as `parameter_endpoint_source` from the shared
// fixtures module (what the read-back parses). They are the same declaration, and
// `test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_fixtures` is the single home of that text; a drift between the
// two shows up as the read-back disagreeing with what this file's own items had to be in order to
// resolve at all.
//
// Run:
//   gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 \
//     --claim-run \
//     --entry dag/test/claim/service_endpoint_supply_module_resolve.dag \
//     --function the_parameter_bound_endpoint_is_still_the_authored_variable_holds
module test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_module_resolve



import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool }


import extdeps.ietf.http_semantics { POST }


import test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_fixture_parse_test { endpoint_shape }


import test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_fixtures { parameter_endpoint_source }

// THE SERVICE AS A REAL ITEM OF THIS MODULE. Two operations, each declaring `request_url: String`, so
// the whole-service quantifier in `service_endpoint_supply` is satisfied. If the admission is removed,
// this declaration is what refuses -- before any cell in this file runs, and at the authored position
// of `endpoint: request_url`.
service module_resolve_bound {
  config {
    endpoint: request_url
  }

  operation GetToken {
    input {
      audience: NonEmptyStr
      request_url: String
    }
    output {
      access_token: String
    }
    transport rest { method: POST, path: "/v1/token" }
  }

  operation GetAssertion {
    input {
      subject: NonEmptyStr
      request_url: String
    }
    output {
      assertion: String
    }
    transport rest { method: POST, path: "/v1/assertion" }
  }
}

test fn the_parameter_bound_endpoint_is_still_the_authored_variable_holds() -> Bool {
  // The entry's own resolution is the assertion that matters (the header says why); this read-back is
  // the reachable half that says WHAT resolved: the endpoint is still the authored variable
  // `request_url`, an `ExprVar` -- not a literal the front end substituted for it. Read from the shared
  // fixtures text, which is the single home of that declaration; this file's items above are the same
  // declaration as real module items, which is what makes the entry demand it.
  endpoint_shape(source: parameter_endpoint_source) == "identifier:request_url"
}
